{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["And the reason for <b>and YHWH gave the people favor in the eyes of the Egyptians</b> is that the people of Egypt did not hate them on account of the plagues, but rather increased love toward them and found favor in their eyes, saying: We are the wicked ones and also commit violence, and it is fitting that the Elohim show favor to you." "<b>Also the man Moses</b>, who brought the plagues upon them, <b>was very great</b> throughout all <b>the land of Egypt, in the eyes of Pharaoh's servants</b> and his courtiers <b>and in the eyes of the people</b> — Israel — after they had said to him, \"May YHWH look upon you and judge\" (Exodus 5:21), and after \"and they did not listen to Moses out of shortness of spirit\" (ibid. 6:9), for he became very great in their eyes when they saw that he was faithful as a prophet of YHWH.<br>And some say that <b>in the eyes of the people</b> means the people of Egypt, and it does not say \"in the eyes of Pharaoh and in the eyes of his servants,\" because HaShem had hardened his heart against Moses and spoken to him improperly now twice (above 10:10, 28), for YHWH wanted him to come and bow down to him as a man comes to his enemy, for all this is greatness and preeminence for Moses. And it is not plausible to explain that <b>and YHWH gave the people favor in the eyes of the Egyptians</b> is the favor of borrowing, for now, at the time of the promise, it would not say \"and YHWH gave,\" but rather it would say \"and I will give the people favor,\" and below, at the time of the deed, it is stated \"and YHWH gave\" (Exodus 12:36)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The citation '(שמות ה':כ\"א)' is normalized to Exodus 5:21; 'לעיל י י, כח' (above 10:10, 28) is normalized to 'above 10:10, 28' following Ramban's own abbreviated referencing style."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:53.480960843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}